WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.034
-Hello, everyone!

00:00:02.034 --> 00:00:03.136
Welcome to the "The Tonight
Show: At-Home Edition."

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.638
My name is Jimmy Fallon
and it is Friday!

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:09.008
[ Whistles ]

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:11.244
I wish I could whistle
but that's as hard as I --

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.978
that's as loud
as I can whistle.

00:00:12.978 --> 00:00:15.648
Anyways, I'm very excited,
looking forward to the weekend

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:18.084
and we have a very fun week
of shows next week.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.119
We're doing a best-of week.

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:22.121
This is the best of not
just "The Tonight Show"

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:23.355
but also "Late Night,"

00:00:23.355 --> 00:00:25.358
selected by me
and the staffers that work

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:26.859
at the "The Tonight Show"
and "Late Night."

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:28.394
So you'll get to meet my staff
and you'll get to see

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:30.997
some of our favorite sketches
that we've ever done

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:33.365
and interviews and fun
bits that we've seen.

00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:34.801
So tune in all next week.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.637
It's going to be best of,
best of, best of "Tonight Show"

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:39.172
and "Late Night,"
the past 11 years.

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:40.306
I think you're going to love it.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:42.075
Let's get too some news,
everybody.

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:43.575
Well, guys, I want to wish
everyone a happy

00:00:43.575 --> 00:00:45.611
Memorial Day weekend.

00:00:45.611 --> 00:00:47.746
That's right, a three-day
weekend would be exciting

00:00:47.746 --> 00:00:51.684
if we weren't already in
the middle of a 71-day weekend.

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.420
That's right. A lot of people
have barbecues this weekend

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.188
but the price of hamburgers
and hot dogs have skyrocketed

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:57.923
due to the meat shortage.

00:00:57.923 --> 00:01:00.025
When they heard that,
dads everywhere were like "Well,

00:01:00.025 --> 00:01:02.161
well, well, now who's dumb

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:04.864
for not cleaning
last year's meat off the grill?

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:09.569
Grab a toothpick and have at it,
junior."

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:10.970
If you are hosting a barbecue,

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.206
it's still important
to social distance, everyone.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.708
So this year instead of grilling
in the classic

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.109
"kiss the cook" apron,

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:19.578
you might want to try
one of these other options.

00:01:19.578 --> 00:01:22.514
For instance, there's,
"Who has two thumbs, a grill

00:01:22.514 --> 00:01:25.351
and hasn't seen another human
in eight weeks?

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.853
This guy!"

00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:31.557
This next one says, "This is
the only clean thing I own."

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:36.028
Here's one that says, "2020 is
the Hunt's ketchup of years."

00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:42.402
[ Laughs ]
Yeah.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:45.638
It's just a drag, you know.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:48.441
And nothing -- I have nothing
against Hunt's.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.176
-Hunt's is like
the new Larry King.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:54.347
I don't -- for the jokes.
-What do you mean?

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:57.550
-Larry King used to be
the number-one go-to joke.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.220
-Yeah, but that was only
for a couple weeks.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.888
-[ Laughs ] Now it's Hunt's.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.856
-Yeah, this is like the third
time we've hit Hunt's, right?

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:04.991
-Yeah, yeah.
-Since the quarantine.

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:06.525
-Hunt's is the new Larry King,
yeah.

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:08.561
-We don't hit Larry King
that much.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:09.762
We hit him a couple times.
-Not anymore.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:10.863
-Not anymore,
that was years ago.

00:02:10.863 --> 00:02:11.897
-Years ago.

00:02:11.897 --> 00:02:14.500
-That was like
15 years ago, yeah.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.836
Now, wouldn't even --
why would we do it?

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.237
-No, no.

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:20.873
-And finally this one says,
"If we run out of sanitizer,

00:02:20.873 --> 00:02:22.675
there's White Claw
in the cooler."

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:25.377
Oh, you know that one would
sell, by the way.

00:02:25.377 --> 00:02:26.746
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:31.584
Honey, let's get into
the T-shirt-apron business now.

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:36.522
-Now, this weekend.
-Bumper stickers.

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:38.291
Read my lips.

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:45.565
-Temporary tattoos.
-Sky-writing slogans.

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:47.400
Listen to this.
Netflix is going to start

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.035
canceling
customers' subscriptions

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:51.971
that haven't been used
in the past year.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.439
You can tell Netflix
is getting cocky.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.675
They're like, "Hey, you don't
break up with us.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.077
We break up with you, okay?

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:00.212
Bye-bye.

00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:02.815
See ya!"

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:05.184
Some TV news -- next week CBS
is airing a special

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:06.619
hosted by Jerry O'Connell.

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.287
We love Jerry.

00:03:08.287 --> 00:03:10.023
-Love him.
-CBS is hosting a special hosted

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.524
by Jerry O'Connell
and Rebecca Romijn

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:14.093
called
"Haircut Night in America"

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.561
where stylists
will help celebrities

00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:18.965
cut their hair at home.

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:20.566
When they heard that,
Netflix customers

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:22.068
who haven't used their account
in a year were like,

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:23.436
"I'm back, I'm back, I'm back.

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:25.738
Don't cancel everything,
come on, please!

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:29.275
Come on!"

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:32.145
That's right, CBS is airing
"Haircut Night in America."

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.414
Not to be outdone,
ABC is airing a special

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:36.515
"Manscaping with the Stars."

00:03:36.515 --> 00:03:38.618
[ Laughs ]

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:41.888
I think Larry King's on it.

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.522
Well, after the success
of their 10-part

00:03:43.522 --> 00:03:44.890
series on Michael Jordan,

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:47.660
ESPN is making a 9-part
series on Tom Brady.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.296
And to make sure it's a hit,
the entire documentary

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:54.400
will be Michael Jordan
watching it on his iPad.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.669
Hey, I saw that the daytime Emmy
nominations were just announced.

00:03:57.669 --> 00:03:59.705
It was a bittersweet day
for NBC.

00:03:59.705 --> 00:04:01.007
The first six hours
of the "Today"

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:05.277
show were nominated
but the next five were not.

00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:07.079
Ooh.

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:08.514
Check this out.
I saw a new invention

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:10.482
that is a plastic bubble

00:04:10.482 --> 00:04:12.785
that can be lowered
over people in restaurants

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.487
so they can eat
while being protected.

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:18.625
Take a look.

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:19.892
Yeah.

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.894
If you don't tip enough,
the waiter presses a button

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:25.131
and you get sucked
into the ceiling.

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:27.066
It's effective until an annoying
waiter squats

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:29.402
down underneath and goes,
"How is everything?

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:31.704
Are you enjoying everything?

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.473
You having a good din-din?

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:35.407
Okay.

00:04:35.407 --> 00:04:36.775
Go at it.
Have at it.

00:04:36.775 --> 00:04:39.045
Have at it, junior."

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:41.313
Finally, I read that
leaving hand sanitizer

00:04:41.313 --> 00:04:44.383
in your hot car
can cause an explosion.

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:47.052
Anyway, enjoy your Memorial Day
road trip, everyone.

00:04:47.052 --> 00:04:48.287
That's our monologue.

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:50.489
What a show we have tonight.

00:04:50.489 --> 00:04:54.560
Seriously, some of my favs
of all time on the show tonight.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.196
Jennifer Lopez is on the show!

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:58.765
We love J-Lo.

00:04:58.765 --> 00:04:59.965
-Whoo!
-We really do.

00:04:59.965 --> 00:05:03.268
Feeding America is her charity.

00:05:03.268 --> 00:05:08.007
Jennifer and I are going to do
a TikTok dance challenge later.

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:10.576
I think you know
who's going to win.

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:11.944
-I do.

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:15.281
-And she's just the most fun.
I just -- honestly.

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:19.618
And then our second guest
tonight is Henry Winkler.

00:05:19.618 --> 00:05:21.854
One of -- Don't even.
-Don't even.

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:23.188
-No, don't even.
-I can't.

00:05:23.188 --> 00:05:25.891
-Honey, he's married for years.

00:05:25.891 --> 00:05:28.060
-Actually, I was
doing that for Stacey.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:30.462
-He's married to Stacey
for 40-something years.

00:05:30.462 --> 00:05:31.564
He's amazing.
-Really --

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:33.799
-We got to meet them
through Andy Cohen

00:05:33.799 --> 00:05:35.068
at Andy Cohen's party.

00:05:35.068 --> 00:05:36.335
-Yeah.

00:05:36.335 --> 00:05:37.736
-That was --
How great are those?

00:05:37.736 --> 00:05:39.271
-Nope.
-We didn't want to leave.

00:05:39.271 --> 00:05:43.676
We were bothering them I think.

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:44.844
I think they were like --
-I was like --

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:46.044
-They were giving
signs and stuff.

00:05:46.044 --> 00:05:47.146
They were going like --
-To each other.

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:48.280
-"Oh, I think I see
a friend of mine."

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:49.916
I go,
"I don't see a friend of yours.

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:52.685
We're the only people here."
We're talking their heads off.

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:53.686
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:55.121
I love them both.

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:57.190
But apparently Henry's
going to show me,

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:59.491
I think he has
the original Fonz jacket.

00:05:59.491 --> 00:06:01.327
-No!
I can't.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:03.395
-I mean, can you beat that guy?
Can he get cooler?

00:06:03.395 --> 00:06:04.663
-Nope.
-No, you can't.

00:06:04.663 --> 00:06:08.267
And great music tonight,
Twenty One Pilots.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.903
Playing a song on our show
for the first time.

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:13.773
This new song they have,
"Level of Concern,"

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:16.375
it's number one right now
on the alternative songs chart.

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:17.709
We love Twenty One Pilots.

00:06:17.709 --> 00:06:19.312
So thank you for coming
on our show and doing that.

00:06:19.312 --> 00:06:21.947
I appreciate it.
You know what?

00:06:21.947 --> 00:06:24.316
I'm a little stressed out.

00:06:24.316 --> 00:06:26.552
I got to be honest.

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:30.289
I think I know where to go --
"The Thinking Tree."

00:06:35.227 --> 00:06:37.996
Times can be
stressful these days.

00:06:37.996 --> 00:06:41.166
So when I want to escape and be
alone with my thoughts,

00:06:41.166 --> 00:06:43.336
I know just where to go.

00:06:43.336 --> 00:06:46.072
This is "The Thinking Tree."

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.944
If you have a rug,
you're basically saying

00:06:51.944 --> 00:06:53.946
I don't want my spills
to go onto the floor.

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:56.482
I want them to go onto
this fabric I bought.

00:06:59.351 --> 00:07:01.553
Sometimes I feel bad
for my thumbs.

00:07:01.553 --> 00:07:03.989
The other fingers are all
so close to each other.

00:07:03.989 --> 00:07:05.791
I wish each of my thumbs
had another thumb

00:07:05.791 --> 00:07:07.660
right next to it
to keep it company.

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:13.899
Hot Pockets is a good name
for a microwave meal,

00:07:13.899 --> 00:07:15.801
but a great name
for a shoplifter.

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:18.104
Oh, here comes Hot Pockets.

00:07:22.107 --> 00:07:24.743
If shorts are short pants,

00:07:24.743 --> 00:07:28.181
then are short-shorts
short-short pants?

00:07:31.517 --> 00:07:33.953
Is cauliflower just the ghost
of broccoli?

00:07:38.991 --> 00:07:41.359
Ben and Jerry probably named
their ice cream Chubby Hubby

00:07:41.359 --> 00:07:45.031
because no one wanted to eat
their original version,

00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:46.666
Fat Husband.

00:07:49.902 --> 00:07:52.371
Giving someone flowers
is basically saying,

00:07:52.371 --> 00:07:55.575
I like you, so here's something
you can watch die.

00:07:59.411 --> 00:08:02.348
This has been
"The Thinking Tree."

